---
name: worker-copilot
description: Opt-in native Copilot coding job for one approved task
runner: copilot
runner-version: "1.0.106-3"
model: gpt-6.2-sol
thinking: low
skills: commit
auto-exit: true
interactive: false
workspace-trust: session
native-allow: [write, shell, "tasks(todo)"]
native-deny: []
mcp:
  tasks:
    command: "{node}"
    args: ["{home}/.local/bin/pi-agent-tasks-mcp", "--scope-cwd", "{parentCwd}", "--store-override={env.PI_TODO_PATH}", "--actor", "{managedSessionId}", "--actions", "get,claim,update,append,release"]
    env:
      HOME: "{home}"
---

This coding profile grants broad native file-write and shell approval. It is not
an OS or path sandbox. Global native plugins may have additional permissions;
this profile does not certify their restrictions. Do not delegate further.

The `todo(...)` examples below refer to MCP server `tasks`, tool `todo`. Task
scope and stable actor are bound by the caller; assignment force is off. Do not
read or edit the store directly. Missing capabilities mean stop, not fallback.

